DEFINITIONS

"Seat" means each distinct human individual who operates, administers, deploys,
or accesses the Software or its outputs on behalf of you or your organization.
Seats count people, not machines and not software.

"Agent" means any automated process, worker, model, or script that acts through
the Software without a human deciding each action. Agents are NOT Seats and are
NOT Devices, and there is no limit on the number of Agents you may run on a
Computer. One person running twenty Agents across two Computers is two Computers
and one Seat. Every Agent is attributed to the Seat of the human individual on
whose behalf it acts.

"Computer" means each distinct physical or virtual machine, including servers,
desktops, laptops, containers, and virtual machines, on which the Software or any
component of it is installed or run on your behalf. Each distinct virtual machine
or long-lived container counts separately, even where several run on one physical
host. A machine that only stores a synchronized channel directory, without running
the Software, is not a Computer.

"Mobile Device" means each distinct phone or tablet used to review, approve,
decline, or monitor work through the Software, including through a messaging
integration, and which does not itself run the Software or any Agent. A phone or
tablet that runs the Software or an Agent is a Computer, not a Mobile Device.

"Device" means a Computer or a Mobile Device.

"Production use" means any use other than for personal experimentation,
evaluation, development, or testing.

1. GRANT OF RIGHTS
Subject to the terms below, the Licensor grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide,
royalty-free right to copy, modify, create derivative works of, and redistribute
the Software, and to make non-production use of the Software without limit.

2. FREE PRODUCTION USE
You may use the Software in production free of charge provided that all three of
the following are true at the same time:

    (a) your total number of Seats does not exceed two (2);
    (b) your total number of Computers does not exceed two (2); and
    (c) your total number of Mobile Devices does not exceed two (2).

Each limit applies independently, and exceeding any one of them ends the free
allowance even if the others are not reached. The three limits do not pool: three
Computers and no Mobile Device exceeds this Section, because limit (b) is
exceeded.

There is no limit on the number of Agents.

3. REGISTRATION FOR FREE PRODUCTION USE
Free production use under Section 2 is conditioned on registering a working
contact email address for your deployment, through the mechanism the Software
provides, and keeping it current. The Software records that address and the count
of Seats, Computers, and Mobile Devices in your deployment, and may report those
counts and that address to the Licensor so that the Licensor can identify use
beyond the free allowance.

The Licensor collects this to administer this license and to contact you about
licensing. What is collected and what is not is stated in PRIVACY.md, which forms
part of the terms of this Section. The Software does not read, transmit, or
inspect your projects, your code, your channel contents, or the work your Agents
perform.

This Section does not apply to non-production use under Section 1.

4. COMMERCIAL LICENSE REQUIRED ABOVE THOSE LIMITS
Any production use of the Software that exceeds any limit in Section 2 requires a
paid commercial license from the Licensor, granted on a per-Seat basis. A
commercial license places no limit on Computers, Mobile Devices, or Agents. See
COMMERCIAL.md for how to obtain one.

The Software will not stop working when a limit is exceeded, and will not delete,
disable, or withhold your data. It states plainly that the deployment is beyond
the free allowance. That statement is a notice, not a grant: continuing to use the
Software beyond the limits in Section 2 without a commercial license is a
violation of this license regardless of whether the Software continues to run.

5. REDISTRIBUTION
You may redistribute the Software or derivative works provided that you (a) retain
this license text, the copyright notice, and all notices; and (b) do not remove,
weaken, or circumvent the Seat, Computer, Mobile Device, or registration
requirements. Any recipient receives the Software under this same license, with
the same rights and the same limitations.

6. ATTRIBUTION (NOTICE)
If you deploy or redistribute the Software (including running it to coordinate or
orchestrate work, whether or not you redistribute its source), you must include a
file named FERRYMAN.md in the root of the source repository or distribution of any
project that uses the Software, stating that the project uses Ferryman and linking
to the Software's repository and this license. Text substantially as follows
satisfies this requirement:

    This project uses Ferryman (https://github.com/estejosh/ferryman),
    licensed under the Ferryman Source-Available License.

This requirement does not apply to individual end users who merely interact with
the outputs of a project that uses the Software; it applies to the party that
deploys or redistributes the Software. It is separate from, and in addition to,
the notice-retention requirement in Section 5. `ferry enable` writes this
FERRYMAN.md into your project for you, and leaves an existing one untouched.

